         "text": "Yaw rate control systems must be robust against variations in environmental conditions such as temperature and humidity.",  
         "analysis": "This requirement points to the need for yaw rate control systems that maintain performance regardless of external environmental changes. It suggests a design that either compensates for or is inherently insensitive to such variations, ensuring consistent vehicle stability control.",  
         "implications": "Implementing this requires selecting sensors and components that are less affected by temperature and humidity changes, as well as developing algorithms that can adjust the system's response based on detected environmental conditions."
      }  
