        "Maintenance Protocols": "Develop maintenance schedules and procedures for recalibrating sensors, including tools and techniques required for the process."
      }
    },
    {
      "ID": 95,
      "Description": "The system should prevent oversteering and loss of control based on limiting the steering angle sensing during high-speed lane changes on highways.",
      "Implications": {
        "System Design": "Implement a dynamic steering control algorithm that monitors vehicle speed and steering input to limit maximum allowable steering angles at higher speeds. This may involve integrating with existing stability control systems.",
        "Safety Features": "Enhance safety by reducing the risk of oversteering, particularly during high-speed maneuvers, through real-time adjustments to steering inputs."
      }
    },
    {
      "ID": 53,
      "Description": "The steering system must include comprehensive diagnostic capabilities to detect and signal any steering wheel malfunction.",
      "Implications": {
        "System Design": "Incorporate sensors and diagnostic software capable of monitoring the health and performance of the steering system. This includes detecting anomalies such as excessive play, resistance, or failure in electronic components.",
        "User Interface": "Design an interface to alert drivers about detected malfunctions through visual/auditory signals, ensuring timely awareness and response."
      }
    },
    {
      "ID": 67,
      "Description": "The Throttle Control system must respond to Driver Input through the Accelerator Pedal within a defined time frame to ensure timely acceleration.",
      "Implications": {
        "System Design": "Optimize throttle control algorithms for rapid response to driver inputs, ensuring minimal delay between pedal action and engine response. This may involve refining electronic control unit (ECU) processing speeds and sensor feedback loops.",
        "Performance Metrics": "Establish benchmarks for acceptable response times and conduct testing to ensure compliance with these standards."
      }
    },
    {
      "ID": 23,
      "Description": "Traction control systems must dynamically adjust to wheel speed sensor inputs to maintain optimal traction performance under varying conditions.",
      "Implications": {
        "System Design": "Develop adaptive algorithms that process real-time data from wheel speed sensors to modulate engine power and braking forces, optimizing traction across different surfaces and driving scenarios.",
        "Integration with Other Systems": "Ensure seamless interaction between the traction control system and other vehicle systems such as ABS and stability control for comprehensive performance management."
      }
    }
  ]
}

